<edge source="russia_ukraine_escalatio::hybrid_attack_frequency" target="alliance_reliability_shi::information_amplificatio" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Surges in sabotage and cyber operations against energy infrastructure generate immediate incident reporting, social-media virality and targeted disinformation that magnify narratives of vulnerability and assign blame.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_escalatio</data>
  <data key="d39">alliance_reliability_shi</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_escalatio::hybrid_attack_frequency" target="global_bond_market_rout::market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Repeated sabotage and cyberattacks on energy terminals, trading platforms and clearing systems force suspensions, raise settlement failures and margin calls, widening bid-ask spreads and reducing the ability of market makers to trade, thereby reducing overall market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_escalatio</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_market_rout</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_escalatio::hybrid_attack_frequency" target="mid_east_gulf_disruption::attacks_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in hybrid operations tied to Russia–Ukraine escalation (cyber, sea denial, proxy sabotage) mobilises and normalises similar tactics among aligned non‑state actors and contractors in the Gulf, raising the measured frequency and intensity of attacks on regional energy infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_escalatio</data>
  <data key="d39">mid_east_gulf_disruption</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_escalatio::hybrid_attack_frequency" target="us_china_strategic_rival::export_control_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in Russia‑linked hybrid attacks (cyber/sabotage) on energy and industrial targets prompts US policymakers to rapidly broaden and tighten export controls on dual‑use cyber, industrial‑control and security‑relevant technologies (including stricter end‑use/end‑user rules that also target transfer channels through third parties such as Chinese firms).</data>
